1 NOTE {geni:about_me} To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110379792/gustav-e-sola
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held in the Ness Church east of Cooperstown Sunday for G. E. Sola, well known Griggs County farmer who died in a Sharon hospital December 21 after a brief illness. Rev. D. M. Rassmussen of Cooperstown officia
2 CONC ted.
2 CONT Sola had for many years been active in church activities and in latter years was a member of the county Democratic committee.
2 CONT Born December 9, 1879, near Stavanger, Norway, he was the son of Mr. and Mrs. Gabriel Enockson. He came to the United States as a young man in May, 1905, and began farming in Griggs County. in 1907 he removed to Steele County wher
2 CONC e he continued farming operations until 1931.
2 CONT On November 2, 1909, he was married to Miss Alvilde Bue. Five children were born to this union. Since 1931 the family had resided in Washburn Township, Griggs County.
2 CONT Survivors include Mrs. Sola, two sons, Maynard of Fargo and Arnold of Cooperstown; three daughters, Mrs. Aldo (Borghild) Iverson of Cooperstown, Mrs. Palmer (Alfreda) Lunde of Upham and Mrs. John J. (Esther) Haugen of Finley; a si
2 CONC ster, Mrs. Leonard Kelsven of Valley City; three sisters and three brothers in Norway; and eight grandchildren.
2 CONT The funeral services included a solo sung by Mrs. Selmer Quam and a duet by Mr. and Mrs. Herluf Vigesaa. Pallbearers were Edwin Johnson, Roger Lunde, Myron Erickson, Harlowe Loge, Roy Iverson and Alvin Swenson.
2 CONT Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Courier, Cooperstown, North Dakota, December 28, 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/view/255/pd00000031778676 Baptism record 1880] - Gustav - parents Gabriel Enoksen and Martha Katrine Knudsdr - living at Utsole - Håland parish, Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT * Gard og ætt i Sola, Utsola, bruk 2, side 454, nr. 1.4
2 CONT
